message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "CSG-KP: A Conformal-Anomaly Resolution of the Cosmological Constant Problem"
abstract: >-
  A single internally consistent framework addressing the magnitude, value, and
  coincidence faces of the cosmological constant problem under explicit stated
  assumptions, yielding one sharp falsifiable prediction: a parameter-free curvature
  fingerprint |Omega_K|/Omega_Lambda = a_gamma/(8 pi^2) = 31/(1440 pi^2) ~= 2.181e-3,
  built from the photon type-A conformal anomaly a_gamma = 31/180 and the hemisphere
  Q-curvature charge 8 pi^2. Includes the full spectral backbone and a Python
  verification suite separating proven from assumed components.
